\pagebreak

=* Abstract

\p[style=Abstract]{
Reliable estimates of traffic density are the basis of ramp metering, travel-time
information and incident detection. This thesis combines the first-order kinematic wave
model with a Kalman filter that fuses loop detector counts and floating-car speeds. On a
12 km stretch of the \city ring road the filter reduces the density error by 31% compared
with detector data alone, and it locates stop-and-go waves within one cell of their true
position.
}

=* Acknowledgements

I thank my supervisors for their patience, and the road authority for the detector data.

